Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer  joins us from Capitol Hill senator good  morning good morning to you all I want  to get your reaction senator to align  them from the president last night when  he when he talked about ridiculous  partisan investigations what was your  reaction to the line if there are going  to be if there is going to be peace and  legislation there cannot be war and  investigation well that line like so  much of the speech just was partisan and  self-serving stacey abrams showed the  president what real leadership was last  night she was compassionate she was  caring she talked about the plight of  her family the plight of American family  she knows the American Dream is out of  reach for too many people and fading for  others did you take that particular line  as a threat I took it that the president  scared the bottom line is that we are as  a country we've always had Congress do  oversight over the executive branch  that's how the founding fathers set it  up senator the president also said that  were he not in office we would be at war  with North Korea what is your response  to that and does he deserve credit for  bringing North Korea to the negotiating  table they haven't had a nuclear test or  a missile launch since their first  summit no but the reports are that new  hood North Korea still has its nuclear  weapons that it may be building other  kinds of weapons and proceeding along on  its nuclear pathway it's sort of a  metaphor the president says one thing  and the reality is another he said after  he first met with Kim jong-un that we  you know that we'll have no nuclear  North Korea of course that's not true  senator apprehensions at the border  peaked in 2000 at 1.6 million in last  year it was 400,000 so there are many  less people crossing the border and yet  the president said last night that we  have a moral duty to create an  immigration system that protects the  lives and jobs of our citizens are you  going to get something done with the  president to make sure there isn't  another government shutdown well I think  the president real  that the shutdown that he caused and  bragged about was a failure and for this  president who seemed so impervious to  what's going on in this case I think he  touched the hot stove and he knows it so  the real answer for the president stay  out of it  we've set it up so that Democrats and  Republicans House and Senate can come to  an agreement and keep the government  open and if the president stays out of  it they're very likely to come to a good  agreement senator let me ask you another  question about the border the president  called it a moral issue this question of  illegal immigration and he said no issue  better illustrates the divide between  America's working class and America's  political class than illegal immigration  what was your response to that well on  the one hand he's saying that we have  more jobs than we've ever had before  and on the other hand he's saying  illegal immigration is taking away all  our jobs as usual the speech is just  filled with total contradictions that  don't add up most Americans I think it's  68 percent certainly I and most  Americans believe that immigration is  good for the country we all want to  secure our border but it's not a crisis  it doesn't demand the government shut  down shut down we've got to go but can  you just say yes or no yes okay the  committees are making progress the  president's got to stay out of it we can  get it done  all right Senator Schumer thanks so much  for being us thanks very much good to be  with you
 

